TipGoing further






Chirp. The carrier density oscillates with the relaxation oscillations, and so does the refractive index. A directly modulated laser therefore changes its frequency during each bit, \(\Delta\nu(t)=\frac{\alpha_H}{4\pi}\frac{d\ln P}{dt}+\dots\) (Henry). Combined with fiber dispersion (Ch. 2), chirp limits directly modulated 1550 nm links to about 10 km at 10 Gb/s. See Going further: linewidth, noise and chirp.
Gain compression and the K-factor. Add \(g\to g/(1+\epsilon S)\) to ld_rate_equations and compute the damping and the maximum bandwidth. Plot the damping rate versus \(f_r^2\) and extract \(K\).
Parasitics. The chip resistance and pad capacitance form an RC low-pass filter (Ch. 3, LED speed) in series with the intrinsic response. For \(R=5\) Ω and \(C=1\) pF, where does the RC pole fall?










